hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16129","He said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub, from Abdullah ibn Shaddad, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us in one of the two evening prayers, noon or afternoon, carrying al-Hasan or al-Husayn. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stepped forward and put him down, then said takbir for prayer, and prayed, and prostrated in the midst of his prayer a prostration he lengthened. He said: I raised my head, and the boy was on the back of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was prostrating, so I returned to my prostration. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, the people said: O Messenger of Allah, you prostrated in the midst of this prayer of yours a prostration you lengthened, so we thought an event had occurred or that revelation was coming to you. He said: All that was not, but my son rode me, and I disliked to hasten him until he fulfills his need."
